From: Project Luma
Subject: [PATCH] luma: every tiling layout has its own id, and the editor's dividers move

New layouts were named after the current event time, which is 0 when no
event is being handled, so several layouts could be saved with the id "0".
Choosing any of them selected the first, so a new layout could be picked
but never used. New layouts now get an unused id, and repeated ids already
saved are renamed when the layouts load; the first layout keeps its id.

GNOME 50 replaced Meta.Cursor and MetaDisplay.set_cursor() with
Clutter.CursorType on actors, so hovering or dragging a divider in the
layout editor threw. The divider sets its cursor on itself and on the grab.

